### CHAP-4iy: Write Integration Test for Transparent HTTPS Tunneling

**Status**: NOT STARTED
**Complexity**: LOW
**Priority**: P0 (validates Phase 1 works end-to-end)
**Dependencies**: CHAP-jds, CHAP-b2i (server and tunnel must work)
**Spec Reference**: PROJECT_SPEC.md lines 46-47 • STATUS-2025-11-28-172146.md lines 165-189

#### Description
Create integration test that validates the complete Phase 1 flow: start proxy server, configure HTTP client to use proxy, make HTTPS request to real domain (google.com), verify response. This proves transparent tunneling works without MITM.

#### Implementation Details

**File**: `test/integration/proxy_test.go`

Test flow:
1. Start chaperone server in test (using config from Phase 0.4)
2. Create http.Client with proxy configuration
3. Make HTTPS request to https://www.google.com
4. Verify response status 200
5. Verify response body contains expected content
6. Verify tunnel was transparent (no certificate warnings)
7. Stop server cleanly
8. Validate all resources cleaned up

**Test Structure**:
```go
func TestTransparentHTTPSTunnel(t *testing.T) {
    // Setup: Start server
    // Action: Make HTTPS request through proxy
    // Assert: Response successful, no MITM
    // Cleanup: Stop server
}

func TestTunnelToMultipleDomains(t *testing.T) {
    // Validate tunneling works for different domains
}

func TestConcurrentTunnels(t *testing.T) {
    // Validate multiple simultaneous tunnels work
}

func TestTunnelErrorHandling(t *testing.T) {
    // Validate error cases: invalid host, timeout, connection refused
}
```

#### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Test starts and stops proxy server cleanly
- [ ] HTTPS request through proxy succeeds (status 200)
- [ ] Response body matches direct request (same content)
- [ ] No certificate warnings (pure tunnel, no MITM)
- [ ] Test cleans up all resources (no goroutine leaks)
- [ ] Test runs in CI environment (no external dependencies beyond google.com)
- [ ] Concurrent requests test validates thread safety
- [ ] Error handling test validates timeout, invalid host scenarios
- [ ] Test uses Phase 0.5 test infrastructure helpers
- [ ] make test runs integration tests
- [ ] make test-race passes (0 races in concurrent test)

#### Technical Notes
- Use httptest infrastructure from Phase 0.5 where possible
- Create test config with unique port to avoid conflicts
- Use t.Cleanup() for resource cleanup
- Set reasonable timeouts (5s for request, 10s for test)
- Test against stable domain (google.com, cloudflare.com)
- Validate logs show tunnel establishment and closure
- This test serves as regression test for all future MITM work

