## Testing Strategy

### Unit Tests
- `internal/proxy/server_test.go` - Server lifecycle, configuration, shutdown
- `internal/proxy/tunnel_test.go` - Tunnel handler with mock connections

### Integration Tests
- `test/integration/proxy_test.go` - End-to-end transparent tunneling
- Multiple domains, concurrent requests, error scenarios

### Manual Tests
After Phase 1 completion, these manual tests should work:

```bash
# Test 1: Start server
./chaperone run --config chaperone.toml
# Expected: Server starts on port 4010, logs startup

# Test 2: Proxy HTTPS request
export HTTPS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:4010
curl -v https://www.google.com
# Expected: Request succeeds, response from Google

# Test 3: Concurrent requests
for i in {1..10}; do
  curl -x http://127.0.0.1:4010 https://www.google.com &
done
wait
# Expected: All requests succeed

# Test 4: Graceful shutdown
./chaperone run --config chaperone.toml &
PID=$!
sleep 2
kill -TERM $PID
# Expected: Clean shutdown, all connections closed
```

### Test Coverage Goals
- Unit tests: 85%+ coverage
- Integration tests: Cover all happy paths + key error scenarios
- Race detector: 0 races (make test-race must pass)

